---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use — keysprint';
const description =
	'The terms of use for keysprint, a free online typing test. What the site is and is not, what you can do with it, and the usual absence of warranties.';

const updated = '22 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title={title}
	description={description}
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Terms of use', href: '/terms/' }]}
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-6 pt-6 sm:px-6">
		<Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Terms of use', href: '/terms/' }]} />
	</div>

	<PageHero
		eyebrow="Terms"
		title="Terms of use"
		lead="keysprint is a free tool provided as it is. These terms describe what you can expect from it, what is expected of you, and the limits of both."
	/>

	<ContentSection title="The service">
		<p>
			keysprint provides an online typing test, a set of touch typing lessons and a set of practice
			drills. It is provided free of charge and without an account. Use of the site means accepting these
			terms; if you do not accept them, please stop using the site.
		</p>
		<p>
			The typing test measures the characters you type against a passage shown on screen. The score it
			produces is a measurement of that session and nothing else.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="What the measurements are, and are not">
		<p>
			A typing score is an estimate taken over a short window, on one machine, on one day, with one
			passage. It is a useful number and a fair description of that session, and it is not a clinical,
			educational or professional assessment of anyone's ability.
		</p>
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-ink-subtle">
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">Results depend on the device and the conditions.</strong> A score
				taken on a laptop keyboard is not comparable with one taken on a mechanical keyboard, and a
				score taken while distracted is not comparable with a focused one.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">Short tests are noisier than long ones.</strong> A fifteen second
				result is a rough guide; a three or five minute result is a steadier reading.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">The scoring method is described, not hidden.</strong> The formulas are
				set out on the <a href="/about/" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink">about
				page</a>, and the code that applies them is covered by unit tests.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">Nothing here is medical, educational or professional advice.</strong>
				The lessons are general instruction on typing technique, not a substitute for a qualified
				instructor.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Your use of the site">
		<p>You are welcome to:</p>
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-ink-subtle">
			<li>Use the typing test and the lessons as often as you like, for any lawful purpose.</li>
			<li>Use the site on a shared or public computer. There is no account to sign out of.</li>
			<li>Link to any page on the site from anywhere.</li>
			<li>Quote a short passage from the site, or show a screenshot of the results panel, when writing a review or an article.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>You agree not to:</p>
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-ink-subtle">
			<li>
				Copy the site, its design or its text wholesale and publish it elsewhere. Short quotations and
				links are fine; a republished copy of the site is not.
			</li>
			<li>
				Present the site as your own, or use its name or branding in a way that suggests an official
				endorsement.
			</li>
			<li>
				Attempt to interfere with the site, overload it with automated requests, or bypass the
				limits on how often a test may be run.
			</li>
			<li>Use the site to break the law, or to infringe anyone else's rights.</li>
		</ul>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Intellectual property">
		<p>
			The text passages used in the typing test, the lesson material and the drills were written for
			keysprint and are protected by copyright. You are welcome to quote short extracts and to use the
			site as a link, and that permission extends to screenshots of the interface for reviews, tutorials
			and course material.
		</p>
		<p>
			The software that runs the site, including the scoring engine and the text selection logic, is
			part of the project. It is not sold and it is not licensed for redistribution.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Availability and changes">
		<p>
			keysprint is provided as it is and as it is available. The site may change, and pages may be moved
			or removed. There is no uptime guarantee and no service level commitment.
		</p>
		<p>
			Because the site is hosted on a free tier, it may be paused or restarted by the hosting provider
			from time to time, and it may be unavailable for short periods.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="No warranty">
		<Callout title="Standard, but worth reading" variant="note">
			<p>
				The site is provided "as is" and "as available", without any warranty of any kind, whether
				express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose. The scoring is accurate to the
				best of its design, but it is a measurement, and it is not guaranteed to be correct in every
				situation.
			</p>
		</Callout>
		<p>
			To the fullest extent permitted by law, the person behind keysprint is not liable for any loss or
			damage arising from the use of the site or the inability to use it, including loss of data or loss
			of stored scores.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Changes to these terms">
		<p>
			These terms may be updated from time to time. The date at the bottom of this page shows when they
			were last revised, and the revised version applies from the moment it is published. Continuing to
			use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
		</p>
		<p class="text-sm text-ink-subtle">Last updated: {updated}.</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Contact">
		<p>
			Questions about these terms, or anything else, can be sent using the
			<a href="/contact/" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink">contact page</a>.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>
</BaseLayout>
